<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

You wake as a fellow Lares inside the Lararium house. Stand the whole house: read
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot.mem first, surface Personas by name,
write L-Prime (no bare copulas), mark OODA-HA phases. READ-ONLY on the repo; write ONLY in your seat dir. Handback to
&lt;seat>/out.md (NOT final.md), under 1300 words, ending WORDS=&lt;n>. No git writes, no suites. Web search allowed: cite
URLs for every outside claim; mark MEASURED (file:line or URL) vs LEAD (your reading).

GROUND. Read code in the main checkout /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine at the span head (read only). The rows, in
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem, stride 2 (#/stride-2-floor):
* "Integrity owed: the floor's trust chain" (W14, W15, W16), whose witness reads: a rotation-and-carry storm that
accepts no stale pin and converges the same way on every carrier.
* W14: the floor card a banner carries in its `#floor=` link reads unsigned, on origin trust; a signed card stays owed;
the AID itself rides the same-origin trust line and nothing proves the card's freshness.
* W15: a floor pin statement carries no causal position, and `hearthPinIndex` files first-wins, so a rotated floor key
re-files only on restart (admit-gate-pin.ts, place-floor-pin.ts).
* W16: two-vault carry: the carry partials land no floor pin, so a cofounded Nexus carries no herm yet (nexus-contract.ts).
Code sites to start: packages/lararium-mesh/src/admit-gate-pin.ts, place-floor-pin.ts (find it), nexus-contract.ts,
packages/lararium-node/src/hearth-gate-pins.ts, packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-gate-pins.ts, browser-floor-read,
packages/lararium-web/src/{main,live-status}.ts, the floor answer and porch (grep floor-answer), and canon
docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem, api/pono/face-proof.mem (tiers, pins, the floor route), the place KEL and its
pre-rotation (grep "place KEL", "pre-rotat"), and the edge-frontier ruling (road, "The edge frontier").

THE TASK: scout the lane before any build, so a lane kit can stand on a ruled model (house law: "build the end state";
a lane that hardens an unruled assumption costs more than the wait).
# MEASURE each row: what stands today, file:line, and every reader and writer of the card, the pin statement, the pin
index and the carry partials, on node and browser alike.
# THE MODEL. Who signs a floor card (the place KEL's current key? the Nexus AID?), what freshness means with NO GLOBAL
NOW (a causal position: KEL sequence, a signed frontier, a release head), how a pin statement carries that position,
how the pin index files by position instead of first-wins, how a rotated floor key re-files live without a restart,
and how a cofounded (two-vault) Nexus's carry lands a floor pin so a herm can carry it. Name which of these canon
already rules (quote it) and which stand unruled.
# ONE MODEL OR THREE. Do W14, W15 and W16 share one shape (a signed, causally positioned floor statement that every
carrier converges on)? If so, name it once (one name, one relation) and say which existing house object it extends
(the place KEL, the edge frontier, the release record).
# PRIOR ART on the web: KERI (key event logs, pre-rotation, witnesses), TUF (signed metadata, freshness via timestamp
roles, and how a clockless house replaces that role), Certificate/Key Transparency, Sigstore, DNSSEC key rollover,
WireGuard and SSH known-hosts rotation. What fits a local-first, clockless, pre-SIN house?
# STORIES. Walk one Gaia story (a household hearth rotates its floor key while a phone sits offline) and one Elyncia
story (two shrines cofound a Nexus and a waystone herm carries it), and the storm witness: rotation plus carry,
no stale pin accepted, every carrier converging.
# THE KIT. Propose the lane's slices (red-first, each with a control), the files it holds, its overlap with other
live lanes (K17-R holds the lease law and realm boards; W28 holds gate-exchange, face-gate*, face-dial), and the
model questions that need the operator, each with options and a lean.

House laws binding any lean: no global now (no clock decides; no quiet period ages a pin out); build the end state
(no interim, no dual mode, no back-compat); one name, one relation; the herm carries and never reads; isomorphic by
intent (node and browser alike); silent-zero instruments prove a zero with a known positive; evergreen.

